Welcome to the realm of the Phoenix.  We hope you enjoy your tenure in this
world.  Many immortals have worked hard to build an exciting and challenging
world where you can explore by yourself or with other fine adventurers.

Classes, skills, and guilds:

When you enter the game the first time, you are asked to select a class; either
THIEF, WARRIOR, CLERIC, BARD, BARBARIAN, RANGER, PALADIN, ANTI_PALADIN, DRUID
or MAGIC user. Characters belonging to each of these classes have their own
qualities, abilities, and handicaps.

It is not unusual that people belonging to different classes, by joining their
efforts and combining their skills, find their chances of survival and progress
greatly improved. Indeed, a GROUP consisting of members from many classes can
be an extremely powerful unit; capable of opening doors without keys, creating
food supplies out of nothing, and destroying an enemy in several different
ways. It is not advisable for a new player to offend the members of such a
group!

In order to learn the tricks of your specific trade, you need to find your
GUILD, which may take a little exploring. However, you can usually find a 
guild in any reasonably populated city. Once you've found it, you need to look
up your guildmaster and LEARN the skills of your trade.  Once you have learned
a new skill, go out inthe world and use it so that you can gain practical
knowledge.  Once you know enough about each skill, you need to return to your
guildmaster to PRACTICE the skill under his/her tutledge.  In this manner you
will become learned and more effective.

Equipment:

It is never wise to travel without the proper equipment. You may purchase
equipment in the SHOPS found in any larger city, or you may be lucky and find
some left around, dropped by someone who doesn't need it anymore, for one
reason or another.  Equipment can also be damaged in battle and must be cared
for well.  You should periodically examine your EQUIPMENT and determine if
it need be repaired.  You will find people skilled in repairing equipment
in most of the major cities, although WHERE they might be might is not
always known.

About Staying Fit - Eating and Drinking:

At one time or another, you'll see the message "You are hungry". This means
that it's time to find something edible before too long. People don't starve to
death in this world, so have no fear. However, when you are hungry, you do not
build up lost energy, so eventually you'll be unable to do anything but sit
around and feel sorry for yourself, until someone comes by. Then, you can only
hope that it's a benevolent person, rather than a greedy thief or a warrior
lusting for blood.

What should you do?

As an adventurer you will want to acquire fine equipment, gain experience in
you skill, and possibly save up enough gold to purchase a house in one of our
fine cities.  As a new adventurer (a newbie, if you will) you must learn
the
ways of this realm.  To this end, you might consider exploring the town of
Heliopolis, home of the Temple of the Phoenix.  The temple halls, just beyond
the western door in the Temple are a fine place to start.  A couple of other
good areas to hone your knowledge of the Realm of the Phoenix are the "Newbie
Area" just north of Heliopolis (take a leasurly stroll out the east or west
gates and explore north) and the Ivory Tower, sometimes referred to as the
chessboard.  You may visit the Ivory Tower by walking south from the Temple to
The Meeting Square and then going west.  You should meet a great and
powerful
knight named Turaylon.  Be polite with hem and use the magic word to gain
entrance to the Ivory Tower.

General Hints:

Again, welcome to our realm and may your adventures be filled with excitement
and your travels profitable.  You will find valuable information at the 
http://www.phoenixmud.net web site.  In addition to the help provided above, 
you should also use the HELP command and read more on various topics.
Typing HELP without any keywords will give you a list of keywords you can
obtain help on.
